# Belt and braces against a seed file landing in the gated suite.
#
# `npx playwright init-agents` and the test MCP server both write `<testDir>/seed.spec.ts` when they
# cannot find an existing file whose name contains "seed". If that ever resolved to ./tests, an empty
# passing test would join the suite the README badge is checked against.
#
# The real defence is structural and lives in playwright.config.js: the agents target the `generated`
# project, whose testDir is ./tests-generated, and `generator_write_test` refuses any path outside a
# declared testDir. The hand-written seed at tests-generated/seed.spec.js is what stops either tool
# creating one of its own in the first place.
#
# This line stays as the last line of defence, for the case where somebody re-runs init-agents
# against the wrong project. It is not the reason the boundary holds.
tests/seed.spec.ts
